# Cached source data and generated outputs - all rebuildable with ./update.sh,
# with one exception: work/gas/gsh_cache is NOT rebuildable. AEMO publishes only a
# rolling 30-day window of Gas Supply Hub trades and nemweb keeps ~95 daily files, so
# that cache is the only copy of every day that has already rolled off. It is small
# (a few hundred KB of immutable zips) and is tracked deliberately.
#
# git will not descend into an excluded directory, so each parent level has to be
# re-included explicitly - excluding work/ outright would make the negation below dead.
work/*
!work/gas/
work/gas/*
!work/gas/gsh_cache/

*.xlsx
*.csv
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Same reasoning as the hub cache, for the terminal gate price series. AIP publishes
# one workbook holding the whole history, so it is normally its own archive - but the
# August 2026 site rebuild republished it seven weeks short, and every build reads the
# workbook fresh. This archive holds the days AIP has dropped; nothing can re-fetch
# them. Listed after the blanket rules above so the negations are the last match.
!work/petrol/
work/petrol/*
!work/petrol/tgp_archive.csv
